T\",\"description\":\"msg and msg_size arrays are adjacent in .bss: msg at 0x4060 (256 bytes), msg_size at 0x4160 (128 bytes), urandom at 0x41e0, cookie_num at 0x41e8\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"The maximum number of cookies is 32 (cookie_num <= 0x1f check in create_cookie, array size 32)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie and read_cookie use signed jl for unsigned input comparison. A value like 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF would be interpreted as -1 (negative), passing the jl check, but the subsequent [rax*8+msg] addressing would compute a huge offset causing segfault rather than controlled OOB within .bss\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F019\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie's idx computation uses signed cdqe+idiv: (int)random_byte % (int64)cookie_num. Since cookie_num is always positive, result is in [0, cookie_num-1]\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F020\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"In eat_cookie, when idx != cookie_num-1, the last element's pointer is copied to idx slot, and the last slot is NOT cleared. However cookie_num is decremented so the last slot becomes inaccessible via normal index checks. When idx == cookie_num-1, the freed pointer remains in that slot via self-assignment.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Whether CET (IBT/SHSTK) is enabled at runtime\",\"reason\":\"checksec does not report CET flags; requires runtime inspection via /proc/cpuinfo or arch_prctl\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether ASLR is enabled in the execution environment\",\"reason\":\"Cannot determine from static analysis; PIE is enabled but ASLR depends on kernel config\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Whether seccomp or other sandbox is active\",\"reason\":\"No seccomp-related symbols or strings found, but cannot rule out external sandbox\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Exact heap layout and tcache behavior under glibc 2.39 for the specific allocation sizes used\",\"reason\":\"Requires dynamic analysis; glibc 2.39 has safe-linking for tcache and other mitigations that affect heap exploitation feasibility\"},{\"id\":\"U005\",\"description\":\"Whether the signed jl comparison in edit_cookie/read_cookie can be leveraged for meaningful OOB access\",\"reason\":\"The huge offset from negative-signed large unsigned values would likely segfault before reaching controlled memory; S2 needs to determine if any value passes the check and lands within accessible memory\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF 64-bit LSB pie executable, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, BuildID=84dab319bf6fe22134cf0338cbd8071fd8bc06c2, for GNU/Linux 3.2.0, not stripped. Entry=0x1110. Type=DYN (PIE). 11 program headers, 29 sections.\",\"sections\":\"Key sections: .text 0x1110-0x19a1 (RX), .rodata 0x2000-0x2266 (R), .got 0x3f58-0x4000 (RW, Full RELRO makes read-only at runtime), .data 0x4000-0x4010 (RW), .bss 0x4020-0x41f0 (RW). BSS layout: stdout@0x4020, stdin@0x4030, stderr@0x4040, completed.0@0x4048, msg[32]@0x4060, msg_size[32]@0x4160, urandom@0x41e0, cookie_num@0x41e8.\",\"symbols\":\"Key user functions: _abort@0x11f5, init@0x1232, create_cookie@0x1399, eat_cookie@0x14e1, edit_cookie@0x1628, read_cookie@0x1751, menu@0x17fd, main@0x187f. Key globals: msg@0x4060 (256B, 32×char*), msg_size@0x4160 (128B, 32×int), urandom@0x41e0 (FILE*), cookie_num@0x41e8 (int64). PLT: free@0x1030, puts@0x1040, fread@0x1050, __stack_chk_fail@0x1060, printf@0x1070, alarm@0x1080, read@0x1090, calloc@0x10a0, setvbuf@0x10b0, fopen@0x10c0, __isoc99_scanf@0x10d0, exit@0x10e0, strdup@0x10f0.\",\"disassembly\":\"init(0x1232): setvbuf(stdin/stdout/stderr,0,2,0), alarm(60), fopen(/dev/urandom), strdup 5 fortune strings into msg[0..4] with sizes 0x50/0x30/0x18/0x38/0x40, cookie_num=5. create_cookie(0x1399): check cookie_num<=0x1f, scanf %lld size, check size<=0x100, calloc(1,size), read(0,buf,size), newline-to-NUL, msg[cookie_num]=buf, msg_size[cookie_num]=size, cookie_num++. eat_cookie(0x14e1): check cookie_num!=0, fread 1 byte from urandom, idx=byte%cookie_num (signed idiv), printf(%s,msg[idx]), free(msg[idx]) [NO NULL], swap-remove msg[idx]=msg[cookie_num-1] & msg_size, cookie_num--. edit_cookie(0x1628): printf range [0-cookie_num-1], scanf %llu index, check index<cookie_num (jl), read(0,msg[index],msg_size[index]-1), newline-to-NUL. read_cookie(0x1751): printf range, scanf %llu index, check index<cookie_num (jl), printf(%s,msg[index]). main(0x187f): init(), loop{menu(), scanf %lld choice, switch 1=eat 2=create 3=edit 4=read 5=exit}. _abort(0x11f5): printf(msg), exit(1).\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":null,\"primitive_reports\":[],\"target_bug\":\"\",\"bug_reports\":[],\"impact_reports\":[],\"strategy_reports\":[],\"final_exploit_path\":\"\",\"final_report\":{}}",
