          "type": "Use-After-Free",
          "description": "In eat_cookie, free(msg[idx]) is called at 0x158e but msg[idx] is never set to NULL. The subsequent swap-remove logic copies msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[idx] at 0x15c6. When idx == cookie_num-1 (the last element is selected), this swap becomes a self-assignment: msg[idx] = msg[cookie_num-1] writes the already-freed pointer back into the same slot. The freed pointer remains in the msg[] array and is still within the valid index range [0, cookie_num-1] after cookie_num is decremented. Both edit_cookie and read_cookie can subsequently access this stale pointer, as their index checks only verify index < cookie_num, and the freed slot is still within that range."
        },
        "affected_functions": [
          "eat_cookie",
          "edit_cookie",
          "read_cookie"
        ],
        "affected_objects": [
